                                    <property name="margin-left">4</property>
                                    <property name="margin-right">4</property>
                                    <property name="margin-start">4</property>
                                    <property name="margin-end">4</property>
                                    <property name="label" translatable="yes">The best manner for setting these is to direct your machine to move a certain distance (e.g., 1 inch or 10 degrees), and then change this value as necessary to achieve the requested movement.  For example, if you directed it to move 1 inch, and it moves 1.1 inches, then divide the setting by 1.1.  You may have to go thru a few iterations of this to get it perfect.

For the spindles, 360° is a good starting point.  For rotary axes, 10° is a good starting point.
</property>
                                    <property name="wrap">True</property>
                                    <attributes>
                                      <attribute name="font-desc" value="DejaVu Serif 10"/>
                                    </attributes>
